  "qualification": "Source-only actual stock Connect consumer activation on its assignment MemoryBudget, preserving captured.allocation. A temporary scalar-only native configuration normalizes four byte limits without replaying unrelated TLS/plugin setters. The pinned absent-fetch queued/message rule, checked native integer products, finite receive compatibility and two-receive-plus-8MiB reservation policy are applied before native consumer creation. Explicit larger demands remain demands; first-large-batch responses can follow the existing oversized-frame error and overlapping admitted storage can independently deny the account. Presence of plugin.library.paths retains its original unaccounted caller branch, not a new unsupported-setting rejection; a one-native-config admission/consume boundary remains open. Native configuration/probe bookkeeping, decompression/shadow storage, individual fetch/error ops, other native allocation classes, log activation, whole-native/Java/runtime and Phase 2 closure remain separate obligations."
